    passage: "FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\n\nHorizon Logistics Closes $1.5 Billion Revolving Credit Facility\n\nHorizon Logistics International (NYSE: HLI) today announced the successful closing of a new five-year $1.5 billion senior secured revolving credit facility, replacing the company's prior $900 million facility that was scheduled to mature in 2026.\n\nThe facility was arranged by a syndicate of 12 banks, with Bank of America acting as administrative agent and lead arranger. Pricing is set at SOFR plus 185 basis points, representing a 30-basis-point improvement over the prior facility.\n\nProceeds will be used for general corporate purposes, including working capital management, letters of credit, and potential bolt-on acquisitions.\n\n\"This facility reflects the confidence our banking partners have in Horizon's financial strength and growth strategy,\" said CFO Michelle Park. \"The improved pricing and expanded capacity give us significant financial flexibility.\"\n\nAt closing, $200 million was drawn under the facility, with $1.3 billion remaining available.",
