    passage: "PROXY STATEMENT EXCERPT — EXECUTIVE COMPENSATION OVERVIEW\n\nThe Compensation Committee of the Board of Directors establishes and oversees the executive compensation program, which consists of three elements: (1) base salary, (2) annual cash bonus under the Short-Term Incentive Plan (STIP), and (3) long-term equity awards under the Long-Term Incentive Plan (LTIP).\n\nFor fiscal 2025, CEO Thomas Greer received total direct compensation of $9.4 million, comprising a base salary of $1.2 million, an annual bonus of $2.6 million (representing 130% of target), and equity awards with a grant-date value of $5.6 million.\n\nThe annual bonus was above target due to the company exceeding its revenue, EBITDA, and return on invested capital (ROIC) performance metrics by 18%, 12%, and 8%, respectively.\n\nEquity awards for FY2025 consisted of 60% performance share units (PSUs) vesting over three years subject to relative total shareholder return, and 40% restricted stock units (RSUs) vesting ratably over four years.\n\nThe Compensation Committee engaged Pay Governance LLC as its independent compensation advisor.",
    question: "What role does Pay Governance LLC serve in the compensation process?",
